{"tool": "finish", "summary": "Every API request that modifies `users` or `feeds` now appends a row to a new `audit_log` table; the last-login update in the auth middleware is left unaudited. Build and existing tests pass; the new behaviour itself is not exercised by any existing test.\n\n**What was added**\n- Migration creating `audit_log` (`id`, `user_id` = requesting user, `action`, `table_name`, `row_id`, `created_at`). No foreign keys, so audit rows survive deletion of the user or feed. `row_id` is 0 when a request affects several rows.\n- `Storage.CreateAuditLog` and `Storage.CategoryHasFeeds` in `internal/storage/audit_log.go`, and a small `handler.audit` helper in `internal/api/audit.go`.\n- `audit_log` added to the `.agentpolicy` nouns of `internal/api`, `internal/googlereader` and `internal/storage`; `@effects` tags updated on the changed functions.\n\n**Audited requests**\n- Native API, users: create, update, remove.\n- Native API, feeds: create, update, remove, refresh one feed, OPML import.\n- Native API, cases the effect tags do not show:\n  - refresh-all and refresh-category, where the worker pool updates the feed rows asynchronously;\n  - category removal, which I assumed cascade-deletes the category's feeds (I did not check the foreign key) and which is audited only when the category has feeds.\n- Google Reader API: subscribe / quick-add, unsubscribe, rename, move, and disable-tag (which reassigns feeds).\n\n**Behaviours to be aware of**\n- The audit insert is a separate statement after the modification, not in the same transaction. If it fails the request returns 500, but the modification has already happened.\n- Refresh-one-feed writes its audit row before the refresh, because a failed fetch still updates the feed row.\n- OPML import writes a row whatever the outcome, because a failed import may already have created feeds. An unparseable file therefore also produces a row.\n- Refresh-all and refresh-category write a row even when no feed is due for refresh.\n\n**Judgement call:** I treated the Goog", "t": 1794464251.17}
